WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.082
"Can we make climate action feel&nbsp;
happy instead of miserable?"

00:00:03.082 --> 00:00:08.720
The current narrative on climate action is&nbsp;
drive less,&nbsp;eat less meat, shop less.

00:00:09.361 --> 00:00:11.066
Less, less, less.

00:00:11.066 --> 00:00:14.672
So we came up with what we 
call the happy climate approach.

00:00:14.672 --> 00:00:18.759
It's actions in the sweet&nbsp;spot 
that not only reduce emissions

00:00:18.759 --> 00:00:22.045
but also make you feel happier

00:00:22.045 --> 00:00:23.772
at the same time.

00:00:23.772 --> 00:00:25.579
Instead of&nbsp;shopping often,

00:00:25.579 --> 00:00:27.208
make shopping a treat.

00:00:27.208 --> 00:00:28.820
Feng shui your fridge.

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:30.417
Catch things before they rot.

00:00:30.417 --> 00:00:35.204
By moving the perishables to the door&nbsp;
and the condiments into the drawers.

00:00:35.204 --> 00:00:37.449
Instead of saying "drive less,"

00:00:37.449 --> 00:00:39.654
we should say “drive more ...

00:00:40.134 --> 00:00:40.790
people."

00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:44.695
Because carpooling can turn those 
dreadful minutes behind the wheel

00:00:44.695 --> 00:00:47.163
into joyful moments&nbsp;of socializing.

00:00:47.163 --> 00:00:48.451
Bundle your trips,

00:00:48.451 --> 00:00:52.794
cutting out unnecessary flights can 
contribute to a sense&nbsp;of time affluence.

00:00:52.794 --> 00:00:55.602
The feeling that you have enough
 time to do what you want to do.

00:00:55.602 --> 00:00:59.429
Think&nbsp;about the actions you 
can take in your own life

